.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH fleetring 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring \- Places, replicates, and fails over SQLite databases across machines you own
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring\fR [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Places, replicates, and fails over SQLite databases across machines you own.
.PP
`serve` runs a node. The other commands talk to a running fleet.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
fleetring\-serve(1)
Runs a node
.TP
fleetring\-dev(1)
Runs a node for development; `\-d` runs it in the background
.TP
fleetring\-stop(1)
Stops a node started in a terminal or a script, after it drains
.TP
fleetring\-context(1)
Names, lists and selects contexts, so commands need no flags
.TP
fleetring\-switch(1)
Makes another context current
.TP
fleetring\-completions(1)
Prints a completion script for bash, zsh, fish, or powershell
.TP
fleetring\-cert(1)
Creates the authority, and issues node and client certificates
.TP
fleetring\-token(1)
Issues and revokes bearer tokens
.TP
fleetring\-db(1)
Creates, lists, writes, reads, watches, and drops databases
.TP
fleetring\-node(1)
Lists, drains, undrains, and removes the fleet\*(Aqs members
.TP
fleetring\-lease(1)
Follows the leases data nodes hold
.TP
fleetring\-orphan(1)
Lists and removes orphans: copies the control plane doesn\*(Aqt know
.TP
fleetring\-archive(1)
Shows and verifies archives, and restores from one with no fleet
.TP
fleetring\-upgrade(1)
Installs another release in place of this binary
.TP
fleetring\-mcp(1)
Serves the Model Context Protocol on stdio, as one principal
.TP
fleetring\-agent(1)
Adds, lists, shows, renews, and removes agents\*(Aq identities
.TP
fleetring\-status(1)
Shows the fleet\*(Aqs members and ring, or one data node\*(Aqs view
.SH EXTRA
Exit codes:
  0    success
  1    the command failed
  2    usage: a bad flag or argument, or a confirmation without a terminal
  3    refused: unauthenticated, or not permitted
  4    unavailable, and a retry may succeed
  130  interrupted

`fleet` is a permanent short name for `fleetring`.
`fleetringd` is the same program, kept until 1.0; `fleetringd \-\-config <file>` runs `serve`.
